# Feature Architecture

Admin features under `src/app/(admin)/{feature}/` split responsibilities by concern.

## Layer responsibilities

| Location | Responsibility |
|----------|----------------|
| `page.tsx` | Filter/pagination state, data-fetching hooks |
| `_hooks/use-{entity}.ts` | React Query reads |
| `_hooks/use-{entity}-mutations.ts` | React Query writes (no toasts/modals) |
| `_hooks/use-{entity}-actions.ts` | User-action orchestration when criteria below are met |
| `*-content.tsx` | Layout, presentational wiring, thin one-liner handlers |
| `services/` | API calls |
| `utils/` / `schemas/` | Pure domain rules (no React) |

## Extract to `_hooks/` when

- The same logic is used in more than one component
- A handler grows beyond ~15–20 lines (try/catch, validation, multiple mutations)
- You need to test the flow without rendering UI
- Modal + mutation + invalidation + toasts are bundled together (see `useAddParticipant`)

## Keep in `*-content.tsx` when

- It's a one-liner (`router.push`, `modal.open`)
- It's purely presentational (skeleton visibility, opacity while fetching)

## Actions hook pattern

When publish/delete/edit flows bundle modal + mutation + toast, create `_hooks/use-{entity}-actions.ts`:

```typescript
export function useArticlesActions() {
  const { deleteMutation, publishMutation } = useArticleMutations();
  const deleteConfirmation = useDeleteConfirmation<LmsArticle>({ ... });

  const handlePublish = async (article: LmsArticle) => { /* orchestration */ };
  const handleDelete = (article: LmsArticle) => { /* rules + open modal */ };
  const handleConfirmDelete = async () => { /* mutation + toast */ };

  return { handleEdit, handlePublish, handleDelete, handleConfirmDelete, publishingArticleId, deleteConfirmation };
}
```

Content component stays thin — JSX and wiring only:

```typescript
const actions = useArticlesActions();
<ArticlesTable onPublish={actions.handlePublish} onDelete={actions.handleDelete} />
```

Domain rules (e.g. "cannot delete published article") belong in pure functions under `utils/`, called from the actions hook — not inline in `*-content.tsx`.

